xt round of auditions.[25] A week after the second audition, Adams, Brown, Halliwell and Stephenson were asked to attend a recall at Nomis Studios in Shepherd's Bush, performing \"Signed, Sealed, Delivered I'm Yours\" on their own and as a group.[26] Chisholm was also invited.[27] The five women were selected for a band initially named Touch.[28]\n\nThe group moved into a three-bedroom house in Maidenhead, Berkshire, and spent most of 1994 practising songs written for them by Bob Herbert's long-time associates John Thirkell and Erwin Keiles.[29] According to Stephenson, the songs were aimed at a very young audience, and none were later used by the Spice Girls.[30] During these first months, the group worked on demos at South Hill Park Recording Studios in Bracknell with the producer and studio owner Michael Sparkes and the songwriter and arranger Tim Hawes. They were also tasked with choreographing their own dan","fieldQuestions":[],"kind":"retry"}]}
